   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the election law, in relation to watchers during election",
    "basePrintNo": "S3141",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S3141-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §8-500, El L",
    "lawSection": "Election Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S3141\n\nSPONSOR: MYRIE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the election law, in relation to watchers during\nelection\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo clarify the process for appointing poll watchers for any general,\nprimary, special or village or town election.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 provides that at any general, special, town or village\nelection, any party committee and any independent body whose candidates\nare upon the ballot, may have for each election district three watchers\nat any one time, not more than one of whom may be within the guard rail\nat any one time. Watchers shall be appointed by the chair or other offi-\ncer of any such party, committee or independent body.\n\nFurther provided, that at any primary election, any party committee, and\nany two or more candidates on the ballot and any political committee may\nhave for each election district three watchers at any one time, not more\nthan one of whom may be within the guard rail at any one time. Watchers\nshall be appointed by the chair or other officer of any such party,\ncommittee or by any two candidates.\n\nSection 2 establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nEach year, the NYS Board of Elections receives numerous questions and\ncomplaints regarding the authority to appoint poll watchers for primary\nelections. Because of where the statutory language is regarding poll\nwatchers for a primary election (EL § 8-500(1)) many have misinterpreted\nthe governing statute. Since this issue generates a large amount of\nconfusion, it is the recommendation of the NYS Board of Elections to\nremove the section relating to the appointment process for primary\nelections from EL § 8-500 (1) and move it to its own separate\nsubdivision(2).\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2017 - 2018: A.1259 (Buchwald) - Passed Assembly 146 to 0 in 2017 and\n135 to 0 in 2018.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
