    "lawCode": "Amd §8-500, El L",
    "lawSection": "Election Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S3141A\n\nSPONSOR: MYRIE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the election law, in relation to\nwatchers during election\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo clarify the process for appointing poll watchers for any general,\nprimary, special or village or town election.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 provides that at any general, special, town or village\nelection, any party committee any independent body whose candidates are\nupon the ballot, and any political committee supporting or opposing a\nballot proposal may have for each election district three watchers at\nany one time, not more than one of whom may be within the guard rail at\nany one time. Watchers shall be appointed by the chair or other officer\nof any such party, committee or independent body.\n\nFurther provided, that at any primary election, any party committee, and\nany candidate on the ballot and any political committee may have for\neach election district three watchers at any one time, not more than one\nof whom may be within the guard rail at any one time.  Watchers shall be\nappointed by the chair or other officer of any such party committee or\nby any candidate.\n\nSection 2 establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nEach year, the NYS Board of Elections receives numerous questions and\ncomplaints regarding the authority to appoint poll watchers for primary\nelections. Because of where the statutory language is regarding poll\nwatchers for a primary election (EL § 8-500(1)) many have misinterpreted\nthe governing statute. Since this issue generates a large amount of\nconfusion, it is the recommendation of the NYS Board of Elections to\nremove the section relating to the appointment process for primary\nelections from EL § 8-500 (1) and move it to its own separate subdivi-\nsion (2).\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2017 - 2018: A.1259 (Buchwald) - Passed Assembly 146 to 0 in 2017 and\n135 to 0 in 2018.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
